{# Decision template: in continuous mode, who speaks next and to whom, as one choice over the legal (speaker,
   target) pairs among the NPCs near the player. The GameMaster has already decided that someone speaks; it
   suggests who, and this choice decides. Rendered into a decisions request, never into chat messages. Sent when
   dialogue.decisions.useForSpeakerSelection is on; otherwise, or without a usable answer, the GameMaster's own
   pick stands.

   Context set by the game: decision_pairs (key, speakerUUID, speakerName, targetKind, targetUUID, targetName),
   decision_speakers (UUID, name, distance, isVirtual, isPrivateVirtual), conversationParticipants (the UUIDs who
   said or were told one of the newest lines of dialogue), sceneDirection (speaker, target, topic,
   newConversation: the GameMaster's suggestion), crosshairTarget, lastSpeaker, lastDialogueTarget, events,
   maxRecentEvents. The virtual-NPC rules and no self-target are already applied to the pairs. Keys are short and
   numbered per request (s2_tplayer, s2_t5); use p.key as given. There is no none option.

   A criterion is one line; profiles and other multi-line decorators belong in the state blocks. #}
{% set ss = get_speaker_selector_settings() %}
{% set tagCompanion = ss.tagCompanion %}
{% set tagInScene = ss.tagInScene %}

[ state last_exchange ]
{% if existsIn(lastSpeaker, "name") and existsIn(lastDialogueTarget, "name") %}
{{ lastSpeaker.name }} spoke last, to {% if lastDialogueTarget.UUID == player.UUID %}{{ player.name }}{% else %}{{ lastDialogueTarget.name }}{% endif %}.
{% else if existsIn(lastSpeaker, "name") %}
{{ lastSpeaker.name }} spoke last, to no one in particular.
{% else %}
No one has spoken yet.
{% endif %}
[ end state ]

[ state recent_dialogue ]
{{ render_template("components\\event_history_compact") }}
[ end state ]

[ state direction ]
{% if sceneDirection.newConversation %}
The scene director wants a new exchange started{% if sceneDirection.speaker %}, and suggests {{ sceneDirection.speaker }}{% if sceneDirection.target %} speaking to {{ sceneDirection.target }}{% endif %}{% endif %}.
{% else %}
The scene director wants the conversation to continue{% if sceneDirection.speaker %}, and suggests {{ sceneDirection.speaker }}{% if sceneDirection.target %} speaking to {{ sceneDirection.target }}{% endif %}{% endif %}{% if sceneDirection.topic %}, about: {{ sceneDirection.topic }}{% endif %}.
{% endif %}
The suggestion is a hint, not a rule.
[ end state ]

[ state nearby ]
{% for c in decision_speakers %}
{% set cinfo = decnpc(c.UUID) %}
{{ cinfo.name }}{% if c.UUID in conversationParticipants %} [IN CONVERSATION]{% endif %}{% if existsIn(lastSpeaker, "UUID") and lastSpeaker.UUID == c.UUID %} [SPOKE LAST]{% endif %}{% if cinfo.isVirtual %} (virtual NPC){% else %} ({{ cinfo.gender }} {{ cinfo.race }}, {{ units_to_meters(c.distance) }}m away){% endif %}{% if tagCompanion and is_follower(c.UUID) %} [COMPANION]{% endif %}{% if tagInScene and ((is_plugin_loaded("SexLab.esm") and is_in_faction(c.UUID, "SexLabAnimatingFaction")) or (is_plugin_loaded("OStim.esp") and is_in_faction(c.UUID, "OStimExcitementFaction"))) %} [IN SCENE]{% endif %}
- {{ render_character_profile("short_inline", c.UUID) }}
{% endfor %}
[ end state ]

[ question next choice ]
Decide who speaks next in this scene, and to whom. `recent_dialogue` is the conversation so far, oldest first; `last_exchange` says who spoke last and to whom.
Keep the conversation among the people marked [IN CONVERSATION]. Usually the person the last speaker addressed replies; otherwise the last speaker follows up, or another participant answers what was said.
Choose someone outside the conversation only when they were named or spoken to, when what was said directly concerns them, or when the scene director wants a new exchange started and the suggested speaker has a clear reason to speak. Someone merely standing nearby is not a reason.
When no conversation is under way, follow the scene director's suggestion if it fits; otherwise prefer a companion, then whoever is closest.
[ criteria ]
{% for p in decision_pairs %}
{{ p.key }}: {{ p.speakerName }} speaks next, to {% if p.targetKind == "player" %}{{ player.name }}{% else %}{{ p.targetName }}{% endif %}
{% endfor %}
[ end criteria ]
[ end question ]
